  "issue": {
    "body": "### Discussed in https://github.com/encode/starlette/discussions/1823\r\n\r\n<div type='discussions-op-text'>\r\n\r\n<sup>Originally posted by **gyusang** August 26, 2022</sup>\r\nWhen sending a CORS request with credentials, wildcard origin is rejected by the standard.\r\nThe CORS middleware handles this case when cookies are included, but is missing the case when `Authorization` header is present.\r\nhttps://github.com/encode/starlette/blob/31164e346b9bd1ce17d968e1301c3bb2c23bb418/starlette/middleware/cors.py#L164-L165\r\nSince Token authentication is also widely used these days, I believe explicit header should be returned when `Authorization` header is present.</div>\n\n<!-- POLAR PLEDGE BADGE START -->\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> - We're using [Polar.sh](https://polar.sh/encode) so you can upvote and help fund this issue.\n> - We receive the funding once the issue is completed & confirmed by you.\n> - Thank you in advance for helping prioritize & fund our backlog.\n\n<a href=\"https://polar.sh/encode/starlette/issues/1832\">\n<picture>\n  <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://polar.sh/api/github/encode/starlette/issues/1832/pledge.svg?darkmode=1\">\n  <img alt=\"Fund with Polar\" src=\"https://polar.sh/api/github/encode/starlette/issues/1832/pledge.svg\">\n</picture>\n</a>\n<!-- POLAR PLEDGE BADGE END -->\n",
    "body_last_edited_at": "2023-08-26T09:25:25Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-02-14T10:33:38Z",
